WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:02.740
Welcome back.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:03.920
Today, I thought we'd do a painting

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.880
that's right out of the heart of Alaska.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.280
We're gonna start with a black canvas,

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.330
which I've already covered with a coat

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.930
of Van Dyke brown and Prussian blue.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.350
And these colors are transparent,

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.380
so it'll still look black.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.580
In this painting, we wanna show the moon in the sky

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.620
with some happy little clouds floating around.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.920
We'll put some almighty mountains,

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:24.100
some beautiful frost-colored bushes,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.720
and we'll see what happens in there.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.900
I'm gonna start with a little titanium white,

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.330
and we'll start right up here where we want the moon to be,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:39.120
and just make little Xs, and just start working 'em around.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.020
You wanna start from the center and work outward

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:45.110
so that the light gets progressively darker

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.710
as it moves away from the moon.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.190
And we'll go out in this direction

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.910
so that it hits the curvature of the Earth

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.810
and bounces back up.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.130
There we go.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.470
Already you should be able to see how the white paint

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.570
is beginning to pick up the color underneath.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.960
We'll just blend this together.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.700
There we go.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.220
Now we don't want to let this get too bright.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.180
We still want it to look like night when we're finished.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.800
Just work it around and around

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.740
and all the way out to the edges.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.290
Do a little over in here.

00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:25.480
Now then, we'll take the large brush.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.970
Very gently, we'll bring this together

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.890
just by making little X patterns.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.250
Mix all the little actions in the sky.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.230
Cross.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:49.420
Now let's put the moon in.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.270
And we'll do that by taking a clean brush,

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.690
and we'll load it full of white paint,

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.420
and we go right straight into the canvas

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.600
where we want the moon to be.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:04.190
push quite hard, push the paint right into the canvas,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:08.680
just turn it, there.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.180
Okay, then with a knife, very carefully,

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.940
we'll take off just the excess paint.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:22.220
Let me clean this old big brush out here.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:29.160
Very gently, this together, let's work it back and forth.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:37.010
and create the illusion of a moon setting up here in the sky.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:43.300
Okay, now then, let's put some happy little clouds in here.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.820
And we'll use the almighty Fran brush,

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.960
and we'll just use this blue and brown color,

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.150
and load it full of paint,

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.880
and we'll take, just using the corner,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.590
and we'll put in some happy little clouds.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.580
Just let one float right across the moon here.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:08.000
A lot of paint on the brush.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.330
There you go.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.180
Maybe, maybe, maybe you can.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.100
Let's see right up here.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:18.740
We'll put another happy little cloud.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:25.630
Little sneaky cloud running around here at night.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.290
Pushing this paint into the canvas.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.640
Really, really work it into the canvas.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.090
Maybe down here we've got some little delicate clouds

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:40.140
that are just floating around, very small little clouds.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:46.670
Just lay 'em in.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:58.510
Okay, now let's clean the fan brush dry.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.000
And we'll take a little bit of titanium

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.770
mixed with just a little bit of the same color.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:08.290
And we'll put some highlights in here.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.330
Just take the fan brush and just work the corners.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.540
Just the corner of the brush.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.750
Just put some paint right in here.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:23.080
There, light playing across the top of this cloud.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.870
Maybe right along here.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:30.000
This is your world, so wherever you want.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:35.240
light to strike as cloud, let it happen.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.680
Let's put some highlights right along

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:42.350
these things right here.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.730
And we're pushing quite hard with this.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:45.970
We wanna, once again, we wanna push the color

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:54.170
right into the material if possible.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.620
Now in this cloud up here, since it's above the moon,

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.480
the light's gonna strike the bottom of it.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.120
So we'll put the highlights on the bottom

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:10.170
rather than on the top.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:16.120
That's a little thing right out through here, like that.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.340
Maybe a little light striking around up in here.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.700
Just a little something playing.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.150
Okay, now we'll take the big brush.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.910
Make sure it's dry and clean.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.760
And we're just gonna gently hypnotize this,

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.000
just to bring it together.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:37.940
fantastic. Look at that. Look at all the little things that happened in this cloud. This is

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:42.900
unplanned. It really just happens. You really can't control what's going to happen here.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:49.300
Don't try to. Don't fight it. Use what happens. Okay. Let's make a happy little mountain now.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:55.940
We'll take some blue and some brown, still using the same color. And we'll draw in our

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.270
basic mountain shape here. There we go.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:13.880
Really push, really forcing that paint into the material.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.540
Maybe we'll make this one come up a little higher

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:25.210
so we can see clouds behind it.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:27.010
Large brush and pull that paint down.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:30.000
This removes any excess that we have left on the canvas.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.400
is we're trying to get all the paint off the canvas

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:45.920
that we possibly can.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.650
Clean the brush.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:55.470
Again, we clean the brush with odorless paint thinner.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.970
Now let's put some snow on the mountain.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.000
We'll take some titanium white and just a little

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:07.000
A little touch of blue, just a little blue.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.830
Okay, and let's let some snow just run right down this mountain.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:15.940
Just let it break and play. This is a very delicate touch.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:25.180
A very light touch. You're almost touching the canvas with a knife. Here's a nice little ridge.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:27.780
Let's let this little ridge just play around like that.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.340
And we'll put a little bit of light

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:40.240
right on this little peak.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:43.270
Just break and play.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.910
Now we're gonna use blue and white

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:48.460
mix to a darker value for the shadow.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.210
We'll start right here.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.810
Let this just follow right along.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:53.430
Let it go.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:05.570
a shadow behind this one.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:12.270
Maybe all the way over here a little shadow.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:19.120
Each highlight needs its own private shadow.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.750
This down a little further.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.890
As you work on these mountains,

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:27.730
you begin seeing all kinds of little things happening.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.760
Use what you see, don't plant it.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.390
Oh, there's another one, I see him right there.

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:40.530
There he is.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:46.650
Okay, now let's lay the bottom of these mountains

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.450
into a little bit of mist.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:51.180
Clean, dry brush, and all we're gonna do is tap,

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.510
always following the angles that we've created

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.880
in the mountain, down like so, just tap.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.640
Okay, over here we'll follow these angles

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:14.520
and tap in this direction.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.000
We're gonna lift up, we're just enough

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.640
to take out the little tap marks.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:35.990
nice little misty effect over here.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:38.870
Just work that right out, and we're ready to come forward.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.370
We've created some almighty mountains

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:43.930
in just a few minutes here.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:49.270
Okay, now we'll take a little more of the blue and brown,

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.060
and back to one of our golden rules.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.290
You need dark in order to show light.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.330
So we're gonna start by putting some dark on here.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.520
We load a lot of paint into the brush,

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:59.730
and we just push some little bushes right out of the,

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:03.170
right out of the brush.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:08.260
There he comes, there he is.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:18.490
Just putting some dark on so we'll have some light showing.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.720
Okay, now we can take a brush.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.550
We'll use a little bit of Magic White,

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:28.010
a little bit of Plain White.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:29.860
Thin paint will stick to a thick paint.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.970
Thinning the paint just a little bit.

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:36.000
Then we're going to push some beautiful little snow-covered trees

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.600
way back in the distance on here.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.980
Look at those son of a guns.

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.410
There they are.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.920
Just hundreds of little trees, little bushes,

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.820
all these things happening way back there.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:04.040
Okay, now we'll take the big brush

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:08.120
and clean it up a little bit.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.880
We have all these nice bushes here.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.120
We need some reflections.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.580
So we take a clean brush,

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.030
just a little bit of white paint on it,

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.290
and we'll pull that down.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.280
Just grab a whole pull.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:23.180
Make these nice streaks.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.860
This is mixing with the color that we have underneath,

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:26.950
the blue and the brown.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:38.490
And these lines need to be straight down reflections.

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:45.760
And a fantastic way to make reflections.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.790
And we'll go across just enough to give it a watery effect.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.410
We don't want to destroy all those lines.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:56.320
We just want to make it look like it's in the water.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:12:00.000
Okay, let's take, lay a little

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.250
a little touch of snow along there.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:06.990
Just take the knife with a little paint,

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:11.070
just put some little snow right along.

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:12.430
Ooh, better get your coat out.

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:16.150
This is gonna be a cold painting.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:22.310
I may have to go find more mukluks and put 'em on.

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:24.270
In Alaska, we have a word for people

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:27.020
who have came to the great country

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:29.390
and have only been there a short period of time,

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:30.000
and it's called

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.740
Chichaco, and if you've been in Alaska less than a year,

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:41.490
you're a Chichaco, so maybe you learned a new word today.

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:43.690
And where I live it's not unusual for it to get 60,

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:47.300
70 degrees below zero.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:52.090
We have a thing in nature that happens, it's called ice fog.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:55.850
Normally it has to be about 30 below or colder,

00:12:55.850 --> 00:13:00.000
and this ice fog coats everything, every little branch,

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.370
Crystals of ice that weigh almost nothing,

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.750
but they create unbelievable beauty.

00:13:06.750 --> 00:13:08.450
Light plays through these little crystals

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:11.440
and acts as little prisms and breaks up the light.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:14.840
You see all the fantastic colors shining and shimmering.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:17.200
It is really something.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:20.240
Okay, here I'm just scratching right through the paint.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:23.360
Make it look like little trunks.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:29.080
Alrighty, let's take the almighty fan brush.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.000
During this series,

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.400
trees with a two and a half inch brush,

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.860
with a one inch brush, and a fan brush.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.360
So, all of these brushes you can use

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:38.840
to create almighty trees.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.050
Today we're gonna try the fan brush.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.650
Load a lot of paint into the brush.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:45.930
Figure out where you'd like to have a beautiful little tree.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:51.070
Just touch, and then just using the corner of the brush.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:55.510
Just begin building some little limbs on here.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.240
There we go.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.780
And we're still using the blue and the brown.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.020
Come right down there.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:08.790
That looks like a good place for a tree.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:19.200
Push some paint right into the canvas.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.440
Maybe we need one over here that's sort of tired,

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.330
sort of leaning over a little bit.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:30.000
In nature, trees grow in every direction.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.090
I'll put another one right here.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:33.930
These trees are so much fun, I get started on them,

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:40.960
I have a hard time stopping.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:48.080
Put another one right here.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.480
As we work forward, we want these trees

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:52.810
to begin getting much larger,

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:57.600
to show distance in this painting.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.000
In so many of the techniques where people paint

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:05.610
rapidly, the paintings are very flat, very overworked, washed out looking. In this technique,

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:16.390
you can create depth that is unbelievable, distance in paintings. And this is how we

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:23.090
do it. We use size, we use color, all of these things combine together to create the illusion

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:27.250
of distance in a painting. Alrighty, now let's do some more trees. We'll put some on the

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.960
other side over here. Put up.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:45.580
This almighty tree up here is very dark.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:48.150
That tree just come right out of your fan brush.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:49.350
Trees live in your fan brush,

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:52.320
but you have to scare them out.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.400
It takes a little practice.

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:56.220
The first time it's gonna be a little touchy.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.540
The next time it gets easier.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.000
Each time you do it, you learn from it, you progress.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.460
I've painted for 20 years and I'm still learning.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:09.650
Every day I learn.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:12.620
Spend time studying nature if you wish to paint nature.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.340
You must understand nature.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:20.880
Talk to trees, look at the birds, whatever it takes.

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:26.830
Okay, now then, let's do an almighty tree, big tree.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:28.070
We'll come right over in here.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:42.220
Here it comes, big old tree.

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:43.570
You got your coat out yet?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:50.270
You may need it here any second.

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:51.950
With the paintings like this on the black canvas,

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:55.650
you can do a multitude of things with this, a multitude.

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:57.990
You can use all different colors.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.000
All you're looking for is a color that's transparent,

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:06.740
black shows through. Use this black to your advantage. I have another tree right

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:17.810
there. There we go. There are a lot of people we have taught to do these black

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:25.540
canvases that are absolutely making a living out of it now. And we have

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:30.000
literally taught thousands and thousands of people to be all

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.980
Almighty painters, to create things of beauty

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.340
they never dreamed possible.

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:41.780
And you can do it too, you can do it.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:43.560
Just jump right in here and paint along with us,

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.220
we'll teach you how to do it.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:49.430
We'll make a happy painter out of you also.

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.270
Okay, I think that's enough trees for right now.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:57.550
Let's take a little bit of white and blue mixed together.

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:00.000
Looking for a dark blue here.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.800
Let's go right into this area here

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:04.380
and let's put some happy little bushes

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.900
and trees back in here.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:12.060
All this is is the shadow color.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:16.900
We put the shadow on first and then we'll highlight it.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.200
And while we get the shadow in here,

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.790
let's put some right into the water.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:27.210
We'll just reflect some of this right in here.

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:30.000
Okay now, let's have some bushes over.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:34.880
Also, just start bringing this painting together.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.200
At home, you have unlimited time.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:40.370
You can come up with all kind of fantastic things

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:41.600
to do in this.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.960
You can put tremendous detail.

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:44.640
Here, we are limited on time,

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:46.970
so we're trying to give you ideas.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:49.100
We're not trying to just give you something to copy.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:53.210
We're trying to give you an idea to teach you a technique

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:57.600
so that you can use this and make unbelievable things.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.600
Back into the Magic White.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:01.590
and the titanium white.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:05.670
And we'll make some happy little bushes here.

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:14.620
Look how that color stands out against the black.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:16.080
And as you work more and more with this,

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.080
you will know just by pulling the brush through

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.720
the correct consistency of the paint,

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.800
if it's too thin, if it's too thick.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:25.600
It's only a matter of time where you can pull the brush

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:29.220
through that paint and almost tell what brand it is.

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:30.000
And we'll just come across.

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:34.730
we're gonna turn this into beautiful little reflections.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:37.420
And while we got the brush loaded here,

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.400
we'll just, let's do this one right here.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:46.040
Big tree here, there we go.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.990
Little more of the magic white.

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:53.340
And we'll come right down here and put a happy little bush.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:55.400
Now let's reflect these right into the water,

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.530
just let 'em reflect.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:09.330
Okay, clean off the brush.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:13.260
That's the most fun of painting, is beating your brush.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:17.920
Good way to get rid of all your anxieties and hostilities.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:23.530
Look at those reflections, but it's a very gentle touch.

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.990
Now we'll take a little bit of white paint,

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:26.710
we'll just put some snow in here

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:28.070
for all these things to sit on.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:52.050
dark paint, we'll put some trunks in, some stems. This sort of gives the tree body, gives

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:59.440
its shape, but it also shows distance in a painting. Use these to your advantage. Okay.

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:04.350
Take a little magic white, make us a water line into here.

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:06.660
Just use a thin paint to make your water line.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.160
It'll flow off the knife.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.920
Let's put some happy little bushes over here

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:33.790
on the other side now.

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.930
And we'll start right here.

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:39.540
Nice one there.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:41.980
Leave a lot of these dark areas showing.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.920
Be careful that you don't cover them all up.

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:50.430
Your painting will get very, very flat.

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:58.410
Get all the snow on those.

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:00.000
And work them in layers.

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:01.880
distance in here.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.960
Do one bush at a time.

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:14.840
Okay, we'll put a few little sticks in here.

00:22:14.840 --> 00:22:22.840
Okay, now then, let's lay a little snow onto this side.

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:26.210
Just using straight titanium white, this is very firm.

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:28.610
And let it break so you have shadows showing through.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:40.140
Just like when we do the mountains, let it break.

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:50.910
Lay the snow in like so.

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:56.270
And maybe there was an old trapper that lived out here.

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:58.320
One day he went to check his beaver traps

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:00.000
and maybe he fell into the river

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.670
here and drown, but is old cabin still here?

00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:04.630
So let's draw an old cabin,

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:06.830
and I suggest you scrape it with a knife first.

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:08.750
Scrape out that basic shape.

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:11.210
It gets rid of the thin, loose paint underneath.

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:14.000
It's also a good way to lay out your general shape

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:17.110
of your cabin, get your perspective right.

00:23:17.110 --> 00:23:19.020
There we go.

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:23.400
Just a very basic shape, that's all we're looking for.

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:26.510
Big thing is to get rid of all that loose paint.

00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:30.000
Now we'll take some Van Dyke Brown, and we'll do the

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:31.680
Far Eve out here first.

00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:44.910
Now, we'll take some titanium white

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:49.490
and let's lay some snow on the roof.

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:57.510
Bring this all together.

00:23:57.510 --> 00:24:00.000
Okay, now we need to have a little snow

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:02.140
other side of the roof, so we'll just take a little

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:08.000
white on the knife and lay it in like so.

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:19.090
Little more brown, and we'll begin putting all this together.

00:24:19.090 --> 00:24:28.670
A fantastic way to make a little cabin.

00:24:28.670 --> 00:24:30.000
If you want to make it look even older,

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:32.800
You can take just a little bit of the white paint

00:24:32.800 --> 00:24:36.640
and let it just sort of bounce along here, very gently.

00:24:36.640 --> 00:24:40.040
Just let it touch and bounce.

00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:43.440
A little more dark to create the shadows on top.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:44.540
Ooh, look at that.

00:24:44.540 --> 00:24:46.340
Look how old that wood looks.

00:24:46.340 --> 00:24:49.650
It's a super way to make old buildings and stuff

00:24:49.650 --> 00:24:51.050
if you ever want to try it.

00:24:51.050 --> 00:24:54.800
Okay, I think we need a door in here now.

00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:57.810
Somebody might come along and need to stay in this old cabin,

00:24:57.810 --> 00:24:59.640
so he's gotta have a way to get in.

00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:06.850
Put some highlights around the door,

00:25:06.850 --> 00:25:09.990
just by using the knife.

00:25:09.990 --> 00:25:13.150
And probably, when this old trapper lived here,

00:25:13.150 --> 00:25:16.690
he's just like all the rest of us, he ran out of room.

00:25:16.690 --> 00:25:18.550
So he probably built him a little shed out here,

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:20.530
so we'll just build us a little shed.

00:25:20.530 --> 00:25:26.820
Just bring a little snow for the roof first,

00:25:26.820 --> 00:25:30.000
just like so.

00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:48.510
dark paint, brown, and we need a wall over here so we just drop it in. Okay, let's make

00:25:48.510 --> 00:25:52.810
this an old slab cabin, so we'll just cut in some slabs here with a point of the knife.

00:25:56.280 --> 00:26:00.000
There we go. Now we can take a little white and clean this all up.

00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:04.210
By now, you should begin having a painting

00:26:04.210 --> 00:26:09.010
that's beginning to take shape, beginning to look well.

00:26:09.010 --> 00:26:14.190
You should be very happy with it.

00:26:14.190 --> 00:26:15.430
And I think we've said it before,

00:26:15.430 --> 00:26:17.880
but painting should do one thing for you.

00:26:17.880 --> 00:26:19.780
It should create happiness in your heart.

00:26:19.780 --> 00:26:22.730
It should make you happy.

00:26:22.730 --> 00:26:26.010
Let's take a little bush right here.

00:26:26.010 --> 00:26:30.000
Just let a few of these run down.

00:26:31.180 --> 00:26:32.780
Maybe another little bush right here

00:26:32.780 --> 00:26:35.570
to sort of push this cabin back into the painting.

00:26:35.570 --> 00:26:39.120
Right along the cabin.

00:26:39.120 --> 00:26:41.690
We need some highlights on this little bush.

00:26:41.690 --> 00:26:45.570
There we go.

00:26:45.570 --> 00:26:48.120
Then we'll cut a few little sticks here and there.

00:26:48.120 --> 00:26:51.320
We're just cutting right through the light paint,

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:56.850
letting the dark show through.

00:26:56.850 --> 00:26:59.350
All right.

00:27:04.060 --> 00:27:11.290
These paintings begin to get close to being done.

00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:14.010
Let's take the fan brush here.

00:27:14.010 --> 00:27:16.170
And normally I would leave these trees very dark.

00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:20.650
I wanna take a little bit of blue and just tap a little

00:27:20.650 --> 00:27:23.520
so you can see 'em a little better at home,

00:27:23.520 --> 00:27:25.010
just to give you an idea.

00:27:25.010 --> 00:27:26.510
Normally I leave 'em very, very dark

00:27:26.510 --> 00:27:30.000
so they really give the impression of nighttime.

00:27:35.150 --> 00:27:40.820
Just here and there, just a few little highlights.

00:27:40.820 --> 00:27:54.620
And just a few over here.

00:27:54.620 --> 00:27:57.920
Ready, I think we're gonna sign this painting.

00:27:57.920 --> 00:28:00.000
Finished, take a little of the thin oil,

00:28:02.620 --> 00:28:05.150
And let's sign him right here.

00:28:05.150 --> 00:28:06.670
I hope you've enjoyed this painting.

00:28:06.670 --> 00:28:08.190
It is a great deal of fun.

00:28:08.190 --> 00:28:11.290
We have certainly enjoyed being with you today.

00:28:11.290 --> 00:28:12.650
I hope you've painted along with us

00:28:12.650 --> 00:28:15.470
and you also have an almighty painting.

00:28:15.470 --> 00:28:16.970
All you need is the dream in your heart

00:28:16.970 --> 00:28:19.010
and the desire to put it on canvas.

00:28:19.010 --> 00:28:21.610
Until next time, we wish you happy painting.

00:28:21.610 --> 00:28:22.650
Thank you very much.
